---
// src/pages/hipaa-notice.astro
// HIPAA and PHI Policy Notice template flagged for healthcare legal counsel review
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/common/Icon.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="HIPAA & Protected Health Information Notice | Emberly Health"
  description="Administrative statement on Emberly Health's HIPAA-aware protocols, Business Associate Agreements, and patient health data safeguards."
>
  <div class="py-14 sm:py-20 max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <!-- Legal Notice Banner -->
    <div class="mb-8 p-4 rounded-2xl bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 text-xs text-amber-900 flex items-start gap-3">
      <Icon name="alert-circle" class="w-4 h-4 text-amber-600 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
      <div>
        <strong>Healthcare Legal Review Notice:</strong> This document represents a sample notice of HIPAA-aware administrative protocols. Federal law does not recognize official "HIPAA certification" for commercial business associates. This copy must be reviewed by your practice healthcare compliance attorney prior to commercial deployment.
      </div>
    </div>

    <header class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-emberly-light-gray">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emberly-orange-tint text-emberly-orange font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">
        <Icon name="shield-check" class="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        <span>Administrative Compliance</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-emberly-charcoal font-heading tracking-tight mb-2">
        HIPAA & Protected Health Information (PHI) Notice
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-emberly-mid-gray">Last Updated: March 2026 &middot; Emberly Health LLC</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-xs sm:text-sm text-emberly-charcoal/90 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-emberly-charcoal font-heading">1. Commitment to Health Information Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Emberly Health LLC operates as a healthcare administrative service organization providing revenue cycle management, certified medical coding, and billing support to covered healthcare entities across the United States. We recognize our fundamental obligation to maintain the privacy and security of Protected Health Information (PHI) in compliance with the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of 1996 (HIPAA), the Health Information Technology for Economic and Clinical Health (HITECH) Act, and applicable state privacy statutes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-emberly-charcoal font-heading">2. Business Associate Status & BAA Execution</h2>
        <p>
          Under federal HIPAA regulations (45 CFR § 164.502(e) and § 164.504(e)), Emberly Health acts as a "Business Associate" to covered entities (medical practices, hospitals, physician clinics, and billing groups).
        </p>
        <p>
          Before receiving, creating, accessing, or transmitting any Protected Health Information on behalf of a medical practice, Emberly Health enters into a legally binding, mutually executed <strong>Business Associate Agreement (BAA)</strong>. The BAA establishes strict contractual limits on data access, permissible uses, mandatory breach notification timelines, and data return/destruction protocols.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-emberly-charcoal font-heading">3. HIPAA-Aware Safeguards & Protocols</h2>
        <p>Our operational infrastructure incorporates administrative, physical, and technical safeguards:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-emberly-mid-gray">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-emberly-charcoal">Administrative Safeguards:</strong> Mandatory annual HIPAA Privacy and Security training for all personnel; formal sanction policies; designated Privacy and Security Officers; and routine risk assessment audits.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-emberly-charcoal">Technical Safeguards:</strong> End-to-end encryption for electronic data in transit (TLS 1.3) and at rest (AES-256); mandatory multi-factor authentication (MFA) on all access endpoints; strict role-based access controls limiting chart visibility strictly to the minimum necessary for billing purposes.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-emberly-charcoal">Physical Safeguards:</strong> Facility access controls at our Plano, Texas headquarters; clean-desk policies; secure workstation restrictions; and strict prohibitions on local storage or external device transfers of patient data.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-emberly-charcoal font-heading">4. Public Website & Form Submissions</h2>
        <p>
          The marketing forms on emberlyhealth.com are strictly designed for prospective business inquiries and practice assessment requests. <strong>Users must never enter or submit patient names, medical histories, diagnosis records, or any PHI via this website.</strong> Any inquiry containing suspected patient identifiers is immediately deleted without processing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-emberly-charcoal font-heading">5. Reporting Concerns & Contacting the Privacy Officer</h2>
        <p>
          If you are a covered entity partner, physician, or administrator with questions regarding our BAA documentation or privacy safeguards, please contact our compliance desk:
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-emberly-warm-white border border-emberly-light-gray mt-2 text-xs">
          <strong>Emberly Health LLC — Office of Healthcare Compliance</strong><br />
          2400 Meridian Park Drive, Suite 310<br />
          Plano, TX 75024<br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:compliance@emberlyhealth.com" class="text-emberly-orange underline">compliance@emberlyhealth.com</a><br />
          Direct Compliance Phone: (214) 555-0147
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
